1
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS.

2
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,840
Please think about it.

3
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,560
I already agreed to pay in full.
I can't keep giving in.

4
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,840
3.98 million.

5
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,080
Not a penny more.

6
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,640
Okay, take care, sir.

7
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,440
It's just a ten-grand difference.

8
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:07,800
Why don't you cave a little, Xu?

9
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,680
The landlord's whole family
came to talk to you.

10
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:12,080
That shows pretty good faith.

11
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,280
I can give it a shot

12
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,760
and try to get them down
to 4.05 million for you.

13
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,880
This landlord's too greedy.

14
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,800
The second he heard I'd pay in full,
he jacked up the price.

15
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,320
Bet you if I agreed, he'd raise it again.

16
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,960
Anyway, he backed out
of the online signing.

17
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,320
Just freeze him out for a few days.

18
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:32,520
I do negotiations all the time.
I know how sellers think.

19
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,680
But his son keeps telling him not to sell.

20
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,640
He says apartment prices
have dropped way too much these years,

21
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,600
so he wants to wait
for them to bounce back.

22
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,880
It's a rare opportunity, Xu.

23
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:44,520
Your boyfriend seems pretty generous.

24
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,240
It's exactly because of it that I can't
throw money around like I'm rich.

25
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,880
Zhu, I'll leave it to you
these next few days.

26
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,440
Please call him more
and help me push the price down.

27
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,640
Let me know if anything comes up, okay?

28
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,000
- Alright.
- Thank you. I'm leaving.

29
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,440
<i>Benyuan, Yuanzhou, and several</i>
<i>other digital collectible platforms</i>

30
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,800
<i>have blown up one after another.</i>

31
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,360
<i>According to stats,</i>
<i>over 300 police reports have been filed.</i>

32
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,960
<i>Public security authorities</i>
<i>are taking the matter seriously</i>

33
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,880
<i>and have launched</i>
<i>an official investigation.</i>

34
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,640
MULTIPLE DIGITAL COLLECTIBLES PLATFORMS
SUSPECTED OF RUG PULLS

35
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,840
ART INDEX PLUNGES 10%

36
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,760
Hey, I saw the news.

37
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,480
<i>Is this you guys closing the net?</i>

38
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:23,880
No. Just a coincidence.

39
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,840
It's actually months ahead
of what Du and I had planned.

40
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:31,000
But with Wen Ruosen
expanding at full throttle like this,

41
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,920
security problems
were only a matter of time.

42
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:37,040
Then the whole plan has to move up.

43
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:38,600
Can I help with anything?

44
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,360
No need.

45
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,600
You have enough to deal with
between your project

46
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,000
and the apartment.

47
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,480
Hold on. I'm getting a call.
Don't hang up.

48
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,400
Hey, Tianna, what's up?

49
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,840
Yeah, yeah. Well,

50
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,320
I'll get it done and send it to you now.

51
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,000
Tianna called.

52
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:12,160
I need to finish revising a file
and send it to her before takeoff.

53
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:14,440
I was up all night haggling
with the landlord, so I forgot about it.

54
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,760
Go do your thing. Bye.

55
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,200
Okay.

56
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,519
<i>Wait, Chi.</i>

57
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,400
Let me say one more thing.
Don't push yourself so hard.

58
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,320
I'm a little worried about you.

59
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,440
I know. I'm fine.

60
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,840
You've got to give me a chance
to learn from you.

61
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,880
You're way busier than I am. Don't worry.

62
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:31,080
Okay.

63
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,160
Anyway, take care of yourself.

64
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,880
Message me when you land in Shenzhen.

65
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,560
Okay.

66
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:56,360
What's so urgent that you had
to come to me at this hour?

67
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,760
I'm sick.

68
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,320
Just spit it out and get going.

69
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,720
I've got a really serious illness.

70
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,560
Have a seat.

71
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:07,080
Let me walk you through my condition.

72
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,840
You want to know
what those bald patches look like?

73
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,640
That was me two years ago.

74
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,000
The company was broke back then.

75
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,000
I was barely holding on.

76
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,440
I was pitching VCs every day.

77
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,040
One day, on my way to meet a VC associate,

78
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,680
I noticed I'd gotten bald patches.

79
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,240
At seven in the morning,

80
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:39,640
I went door to door at hair salons,

81
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,280
begging them to shave my head.

82
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,400
What does this have to do
with your illness?

83
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,840
Let me finish.

84
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:50,640
OUTPATIENT RECORD

85
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,760
This is my diagnosis report.

86
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,640
I've got a really severe stomach ulcer.

87
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,080
My stomach's a mess.

88
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,200
I wish I could lock myself
in the bathroom 24/7

89
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,640
and be stuck at home for days.

90
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,520
This is my ID,

91
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,120
my household register, and my diploma.

92
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,280
This is my family.

93
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,920
My parents divorced when I was little.

94
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,600
My dad ran off with someone else.

95
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,680
And I never had a great relationship
with my stepdad.

96
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,480
These are my two best friends.

97
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,600
My ride-or-dies.

98
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,720
And…

99
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,080
lastly,

100
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,520
I want to introduce you

101
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,800
to my favorite, Sun Wukong.

102
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,200
Since third grade,

103
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,480
I've taken him everywhere I go.

104
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:49,680
I'm done.

105
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,440
I've listened to all this,
and I still don't get it.

106
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,880
What does any of this have to do with me?

107
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:02,960
Of course it does.

108
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,840
You wouldn't accept me

109
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,400
because you wanted to keep your dignity.

110
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,320
I finally figured it out.

111
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,840
It's just because when we first met,

112
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,120
your work wasn't going well.

113
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:16,120
Every day you were either
dealing with your divorce

114
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,400
or running to the hospital.

115
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,960
You showed me all your worst moments.

116
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,240
So it made you feel really awkward.

117
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,360
Now I've shown you
the realest version of me.

118
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,160
And I'm telling you,
I've got plenty of mess too.

119
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,080
Now we're even.

120
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,680
I'm really not as glamorous as you think.

121
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,760
I've had my ugly, pathetic moments too.

122
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:37,240
Every morning I woke up
to a mountain of mess.

123
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,800
Let me be straight with you.

124
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,720
Because of Bolo,

125
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,880
my apartment's
still mortgaged to the bank.

126
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,320
If one day Bolo blows up
like those digital collectible platforms,

127
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,360
I might not even

128
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:50,080
have money for a hair transplant.

129
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,280
I'm telling you all this

130
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,040
because I want you to know…

131
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:05,480
I really like you.

132
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,680
I used to like

133
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,800
the tough act you put on.

134
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,080
Now I like the you who,

135
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,680
even after being knocked down
a thousand times,

136
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:21,480
still gets back up
and tries to live a beautiful life.

137
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,320
Can you give me a chance?

138
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,440
And give yourself one too?

139
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,880
You bring your lipstick,
and I'll bring my toys.

140
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:38,480
Let's have some drinks
and get some hot pot.

141
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:41,480
Let's go on a nice trip.
That's better than anything.

142
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:42,799
Stop.

143
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,040
Okay.

144
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,440
I won't say anything.

145
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,080
I'll show you.

146
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,800
- Morning.
- Morning.

147
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,200
MESSAGE

148
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,600
FIRST TIME I'M ACTUALLY THANKFUL
FOR MY MOTHER SETTING UP THAT BLIND DATE

149
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,240
Who even sends MMS these days.

150
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:08,640
<i>First time I'm actually thankful</i>
<i>for my mother setting up that blind date.</i>

151
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:11,520
<i>Beautiful Tianna, nice to meet you.</i>

152
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,680
<i>Blind date?</i>

153
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,880
What's wrong with you?
You've been acting weird all morning.

154
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,440
Didn't sleep well last night.

155
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,240
Stop lying. You've never
treated me like this before.

156
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,280
It's really nothing.

157
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,000
You're really pushing it now?

158
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,520
Tell me what's going on right now
or we're breaking up.

159
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,040
Fine.

160
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,560
Were we ever even together?

161
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,320
Then how can we break up?

162
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:27,760
What's wrong with you?

163
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,640
FIRST TIME I'M ACTUALLY THANKFUL
FOR MY MOTHER SETTING UP THAT BLIND DATE

164
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,560
BEAUTIFUL TIANNA, NICE TO MEET YOU

165
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,200
Let me explain. Here's the thing.

166
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,240
I did have a meal with Shen Jin.

167
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,840
And I did joke around
with him a bit about Lin.

168
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,360
- And then…
- Were you two on a date?

169
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,240
Are you interrogating me?

170
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,160
You know

171
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:56,520
my family has certain
social obligations we can't avoid.

172
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,880
Don't be like this, okay?

173
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,800
Something just occurred to me.

174
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,320
I've got two good friends.

175
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,240
Both total characters.

176
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,720
One's a scheming guy.

177
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,960
He knows his girlfriend
is going on blind dates,

178
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:12,280
and he still acts like nothing's wrong
and treats her all sweet.

179
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,960
He took advantage of her guilt,

180
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,800
slept with her,
got her pregnant, married her,

181
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,280
and called it a win.

182
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,160
My other friend is pretty average.

183
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:24,120
He takes things personally.
He gets upset, he gets angry,

184
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,640
and he starts wondering

185
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,840
what kind of relationship
he and his girlfriend actually have

186
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:30,200
when, after all this time,
she still won't acknowledge him

187
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:32,240
in front of her colleagues and friends.

188
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,400
She even

189
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:36,400
thinks going on blind dates
is just normal socializing.

190
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,720
Aren't my two friends interesting?

191
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:41,400
If you were me, which one would you pick?

192
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:47,960
They're definitely interesting.

193
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,440
Right?

194
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,240
So you want to fight?

195
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,480
Then let me ask you,

196
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,160
isn't Xu Chi our friend?

197
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,680
Doesn't she know about us?

198
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,120
- And Ye Xinzhi also--
- I really don't wanna fight.

199
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,240
I just want you to tell me

200
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,840
which of these two versions

201
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,960
of Zhao Heng you prefer.

202
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,680
You--

203
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:38,520
Shen Jin, tell me straight.
What are you getting at?

204
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,880
Hold on.

205
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,600
You'll be thanking me later.

206
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:44,560
BU TIANNA, MAXMISE

207
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:45,880
Hello?

208
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,560
- Wen Ruosen's had a tough run lately.
- What happened?

209
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,760
He's about to face criminal charges.

210
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:22,720
- Really?
- Yeah. Look.

211
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,960
After getting sued, he got dragged

212
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,160
into a bunch of platform blowups?

213
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,440
Yeah. On top of that,

214
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:30,960
buyers are flocking
to his gallery to protest,

215
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,680
claiming he and the platforms
ran a rat trading scheme.

216
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:37,480
Excuse me. Can I borrow
your phone for a sec?

217
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:40,640
Thanks.

218
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:48,960
Thanks.

219
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,080
Xinzhi, it's me. The Yuanzhou thing…

220
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:05,840
<i>Yeah, this time it was us.</i>

221
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,360
Du's team was monitoring public opinion

222
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,400
and saw people
going to the gallery to protest,

223
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,800
so they pushed a few trending topics.

224
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:14,160
I was just about to tell you.

225
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,520
I sat in on a local CBIRC meeting
this morning.

226
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,680
<i>A bank mentioned</i>
<i>they're pulling loans from several</i>

227
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:20,120
<i>collectible companies</i>
<i>with bad reputations.</i>

228
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,640
Yuanzhou is one of them.

229
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:24,200
Got it. With this intel,

230
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:27,200
I can go tip off
Wen Ruosen's lending bank in Beijing.

231
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:31,680
So? Officer Rabbit's
pretty impressive, huh?

232
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:33,000
Impressive.

233
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:35,040
When I got handcuffed, I was terrified.

234
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:38,000
You're a bad guy. Talk to you later.

235
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,640
I have to work a bit more.

236
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,760
- Let's meet when I'm back.
- <i>By the way,</i>

237
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,200
<i>how do you get to sit in</i>
<i>on finance sector meetings?</i>

238
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,400
You went to Celestial again?

239
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,520
I had no choice.
The project's wrapping up.

240
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,960
Final delivery's next week.

241
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,160
So I'm just going nonstop.

242
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,760
I've only slept about six hours
these past two days.

243
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,680
In half an hour, I'm heading
to the airport to fly to Chengdu.

244
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,040
It's really satisfying, though.

245
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,280
I've been on the road
and already finished deliveries

246
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,280
for two branch offices.

247
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,720
But Tianna

248
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,080
is not having a great day.

249
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,760
A file she delivered got rejected
by Celestial again.

250
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,720
She's putting on a brave face,

251
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,160
but I know she's crushed inside.

252
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:20,000
Send me your location.

253
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,960
Why?

254
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,080
The sly old fox
wants to treat his little rabbit

255
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:24,240
to a luxury ride,

256
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,080
complete with a zero-gravity seat

257
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,720
for some real sleep. Is that okay?

258
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,120
Thank you.

259
