or missed my flight.

363
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:42,760
Do me this solid, okay?

364
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,120
Is she really that important?

365
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:48,760
More important than the revenge
you've waited years for?

366
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,000
Yes.

367
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,120
Because my hatred for Wen Ruosen
is in the past.

368
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,440
But she

369
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:57,560
is my future.

370
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:00,080
HAZARDOUS WORK IN PROGRESS
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

371
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:02,840
‪-Everyone, please calm down.
‪-My stuff is still in there!

372
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,920
‪-Everything is under inspection now.
‪-Please let us in.

373
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,120
‪-Please move back a little.
‪-What are we supposed to do?

374
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:10,280
‪-Please step back. Don't push.
‪-Let us in!

375
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:13,600
‪We will come up with a solution.
‪Everyone, please stay calm.

376
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,200
‪Please step back for safety.
‪It's very dangerous.

377
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:19,520
‪Why is everything being taken away?

378
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:20,600
‪Stop pushing!

379
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,160
‪Don't crowd.

380
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,880
‪Step back a little.

381
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:30,520
Chi.

382
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:32,320
What's wrong?

383
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:35,520
Chi? Chi?

384
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,480
Chi, are you okay?

385
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,840
Chi, there are too many people here.

386
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,360
Let's go home, alright?

387
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:46,720
Let's go home, alright?

388
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,000
What did you say?

389
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:53,080
I can't hear you.

390
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:55,480
You can't hear?

391
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:59,160
What's wrong? Chi!

392
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:03,440
Chi!

393
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:05,080
Chi!

394
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:09,600
How did the meeting go?

395
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:13,120
Don't worry. I've got no objections.

396
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,440
I'll be there next time for sure.

397
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:18,160
<i>How's your little girl doing?</i>

398
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,800
She just got the IV.
Still hasn't come around.

399
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,560
She's awake, but she's still not stable.

400
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,080
- Come take a look.
- Hang on a sec!

401
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:28,320
Have you seen my laptop?

402
00:24:29,120 --> 00:24:30,160
- My laptop…
- You're awake.

403
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:32,240
You've got barotrauma of the ear.

404
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:33,520
The doctor said they've treated you.

405
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:36,160
- What did you say? I can't hear you.
- She still can't hear?

406
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,520
- No, we still need to monitor her.
- What's wrong with me?

407
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,720
What's wrong with my ears? I can't hear!

408
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:42,280
- Am I okay?
- You're fine.

409
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:52,480
YOU'VE GOT EAR BAROTRAUMA
THE DOCTOR SAID THEY'VE TREATED YOU

410
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,120
BUT YOU NEED TO REST
I'M HERE. DON'T BE SCARED

411
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:01,120
I'm fine. I'm not scared.

412
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:04,360
I'm healthy. I'll definitely be fine
after some sleep.

413
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:05,520
Yeah, yeah.

414
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:08,400
Where's my laptop?
It's got the files I just revised.

415
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,280
- It's here.
- I need to go to the office tomorrow.

416
00:25:10,360 --> 00:25:12,040
- Yeah, yeah.
- Let me go back, okay?

417
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,800
Don't be scared. Just rest.

418
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:14,760
I'll stay with you. Listen to me, alright?

419
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:22,880
I AM HERE WITH YOU

420
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,240
I AM HERE

421
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:32,160
ALRIGHT?

422
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:47,960
EMERGENCY ROOM

423
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:02,680
I'll stay with you.

424
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:07,040
Sleep.

425
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:52,720
BAROTRAUMA OF THE EAR

426
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:57,200
BAROTRAUMATIC OTITIS MEDIA

427
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,560
EUSTACHIAN TUBE DYSFUNCTION
RAPID EXTERNAL PRESSURE CHANGES

428
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:06,680
Scumbag.

429
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:08,760
Scum… Scumbag.

430
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:16,560
I've got nothing left!

431
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:18,320
You've got me.

432
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:22,400
<i>Chi, I've got nothing left.</i>

433
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:27,560
Now I can't hear, just like you.

434
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:30,040
Let it all out. Cry.

435
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:31,840
I'm right here.

436
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:29,840
See that?

437
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,440
You were awesome just now.

438
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:33,800
Right?

439
00:31:40,560 --> 00:31:41,800
You know why I'm so accurate?

440
00:31:42,320 --> 00:31:43,320
Why?

441
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,360
Is bowling good for this too?

442
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:49,320
You know why I'm good at bowling?

443
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:50,680
Why?

444
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:52,560
Feel it.

445
00:31:54,320 --> 00:31:55,640
I've felt it before.

446
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:01,680
We're out having fun.

447
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:03,480
I'm not out having fun.

448
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:05,560
I'm here for work.
You insisted on tagging along.

449
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:08,240
I moved my conference call to noon

450
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:11,200
just so I'd have an excuse
to sneak out and see you.

451
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:13,600
We just got together.

452
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:15,480
There's gotta be
some romance to it, right?

453
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:16,840
If you ask me,

454
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,800
why don't you just quit Maxmise?

455
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:19,720
Join my company.

456
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:25,280
Shen Jin, I thought

457
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,480
you were different from my ex-husband.

458
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:30,120
Come on. I was just saying it
off the top of my head.

459
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:32,680
You know how strong Bolo is.

460
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,920
I just don't want you working so hard.

461
00:32:35,680 --> 00:32:39,000
But I don't like people
planning out my life. Okay?

462
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:42,800
Sure.

463
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,600
Sure.

464
00:33:14,280 --> 00:33:15,320
Xinzhi!

465
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:17,480
Xinzhi, where's my laptop bag?

466
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:18,720
- I need to go to the office.
- Forget the laptop.

467
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,080
I asked Sha Sha for the day off for you.

468
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:23,240
No. I've got a meeting at 9:10.

469
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,000
You can hear now?

470
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:32,200
She still has some ringing
and fullness in her ears.

471
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:34,040
But she can communicate fine.

472
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:36,840
37.9 degrees Celsius.

473
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:41,480
It's good to be young. Recovers so fast.

474
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,360
Alright, Dr. Liu. Don't worry.

475
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:45,240
I'll bring her over
for her IV this afternoon.

476
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:49,400
No work.

477
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:52,000
I'm fine now.
This meeting's really important.

478
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:55,400
Dr. Liu said normal turbulence
wouldn't cause barotrauma.

479
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:56,440
Your ear problem

480
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:58,960
is definitely from fatigue or stress.

481
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:00,680
I'm fine now.

482
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:03,480
I've got meetings today too.

483
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:05,760
Even I can take a day off.
Why don't you try it?

484
00:34:06,360 --> 00:34:08,159
Take a break.
The world won't stop turning.

485
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:11,800
Here.

486
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:13,480
Enjoy.

487
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:40,760
Chi.

488
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:43,800
I really need to have
a serious talk with you.

489
00:34:45,280 --> 00:34:46,400
I know what you're gonna say.

490
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:48,040
I've actually already summed it up myself.

491
00:34:48,719 --> 00:34:51,760
My biggest problem this time
was that I was overconfident.

492
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:54,639
You kept telling me
to seize the opportunity and act fast.

493
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:57,280
But I wasn't happy
that the landlord raised the price,

494
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:59,760
and I wanted to show off
my negotiating skills,

495
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:01,760
and I forgot to keep an eye
on what was going on outside.

496
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,040
That's what led to all this.

497
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:08,880
Chi.

498
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:10,600
I'm your boyfriend,

499
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:11,600
not your boss.

500
00:35:11,680 --> 00:35:13,120
No need to report every mistake to me.

501
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,720
I know. I'm not.

502
00:35:21,960 --> 00:35:23,560
But good thing
the place didn't go through.

503
00:35:24,400 --> 00:35:26,080
Otherwise, it'd be deemed unsafe,

504
00:35:26,600 --> 00:35:27,840
and your money
would've gone down the drain.

505
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:29,880
Money doesn't matter at all.

506
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:32,200
Your health is what matters most.

507
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:34,600
Your ears are already acting up.
That's life giving you a warning.

508
00:35:34,680 --> 00:35:36,520
You can't keep doing this,
or you're really gonna crash.

509
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:39,520
But I already promised you
I wouldn't go to work today.

510
00:35:40,120 --> 00:35:41,200
Not just today.

511
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,320
You're too driven.

512
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:44,640
You want to win at everything.

513
00:35:44,720 --> 00:35:46,800
You're secretly competing with Bu Tianna.

514
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:49,120
Is it really that hard to accept

515
00:35:49,200 --> 00:35:50,520
that she became project manager first?

516
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,320
Nobody goes through life
without ever failing.

517
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:57,320
A consultant who's never
gotten used to being surpassed

518
00:35:57,840 --> 00:35:59,120
isn't really a seasoned pro.

519
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:08,040
But I already failed.

520
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:12,320
The agent said
an unsafe building can't be sold.

521
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:15,040
I'll never be able to buy
my mom's apartment back.

522
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,840
How did you fail?

523
00:36:16,920 --> 00:36:19,160
Is that apartment
really that important to you?

524
00:36:19,240 --> 00:36:20,960
Of course it is.

525
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:23,560
It's the place my mom
always dreamed about.

526
00:36:23,640 --> 00:36:24,880
It's my whole sense of security.

527
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,800
From an outsider's perspective,

528
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:29,640
that apartment can't give you
security anymore.

529
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:32,880
Before, whenever something happened,

530
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,560
you'd go hole up in that place.

531
00:36:35,640 --> 00:36:37,800
But recently, during your leave,

532
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:38,760
you never went there.

533
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:42,680
And when you got busy,
you'd even forget to call the agent back.

534
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:44,400
Chi,

535
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:46,480
is that apartment
really that irreplaceable?

536
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:49,880
What was your mom's last wish, really?

537
00:36:50,560 --> 00:36:52,040
Did she make you promise
to buy that apartment back?

538
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:01,280
Before my mom passed,

539
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:03,440
all she wanted was for me to be okay.

540
00:37:05,040 --> 00:37:06,120
Exactly.

541
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:09,400
That was a goal you set for yourself,

542
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:11,880
a shackle you put on yourself.

543
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:15,400
Your mom would've wanted you
to live happy and healthy

544
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:16,600
every day,

545
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,280
not worn out like this.

546
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:23,680
But without that apartment as my goal,

547
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,960
I don't know what the point of my life is.

548
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:29,000
You tell me not to push so hard,

549
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:32,160
but if I don't work overtime,
I don't know where to go.

550
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:41,080
Come with me.

551
00:37:50,440 --> 00:37:52,480
You know why I rented a place here?

552
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:54,560
Because from here,

553
00:37:54,640 --> 00:37:57,200
you can see the city's bustling CBD.

554
00:37:57,280 --> 00:37:59,480
And it lets you feel
the everyday world too.

555
00:38:00,080 --> 00:38:02,400
Look over there. Those old trees.

556
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:04,120
When spring comes,

557
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:07,080
the peach, pear,
and crabapple trees are all in bloom.

558
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,080
Any quick phone snap turns out amazing.

559
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:14,640
That alley over there
has my favorite barbershop.

560
00:38:14,720 --> 00:38:17,280
The stylist in there talks way too much,

561
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:18,840
but he's great at actual haircuts.

562
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:21,960
And by that patch of green over there,

563
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:25,320
there is a really great baozi shop.

564
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:26,640
Really juicy.

565
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:28,160
One bite and it's burning hot,

566
00:38:28,240 --> 00:38:29,520
but so savory.

567
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:33,280
Chi, have you ever
experienced any of this?

568
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,360
My life…

569
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:44,880
is basically just

570
00:38:45,840 --> 00:38:48,400
offices, hotels,

571
00:38:48,960 --> 00:38:50,200
office buildings, and airports.

572
00:38:50,800 --> 00:38:51,760
Then I'll show you from now on.

573
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:54,600
Truth is, there are

574
00:38:54,680 --> 00:38:57,000
so many simple, everyday things in life

575
00:38:57,880 --> 00:38:59,280
that we just need to make
an effort to appreciate.

576
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:04,760
Forget about that old apartment.

577
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:08,360
Let me give you
that sense of security. Alright?

578
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:17,920
I bought it ages ago.
At the jewelry store right next to P&J.

579
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:19,280
The place we first met.

580
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:53,720
Will you marry me?

581
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,400
Please don't think

582
00:39:58,480 --> 00:39:59,840
I'm making a move
because you're vulnerable.

583
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:11,400
I…

584
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:16,160
I'm really happy.

585
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:20,640
But I don't think I'm ready yet.

586
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:29,720
Knew you'd say that.

587
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:31,120
It's a two-in-one.

588
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,200
You can wear it for now.

589
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:40,920
Whenever you're ready, just tell me.

590
00:40:58,280 --> 00:40:59,240
It's on.

591
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,040
Do you like it?

592
00:41:21,040 --> 00:41:22,240
Thank you.

593
00:41:24,240 --> 00:41:26,560
I also have myself to thank.

594
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:30,320
Back at that interview,

595
00:41:31,040 --> 00:41:33,640
I outperformed and moved the heavens…

596
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:37,640
which is how I got to meet you.

597
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:23,360
That's the delivery
I completed for Celestial's

598
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:26,760
four branch offices in the form
of training and workshops. Thank you.

599
00:42:37,360 --> 00:42:39,880
If there are no issues,
that's a wrap for today's meeting.

600
00:42:43,160 --> 00:42:45,320
Miss Xu, thank you.

601
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:46,400
No worries.

602
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,120
Tianna.

603
00:42:50,120 --> 00:42:52,600
Hope the rest of the delivery goes
as smoothly and efficiently as today's.

604
00:42:54,520 --> 00:42:55,960
Please rest assured. I'll get it done.

605
00:42:57,480 --> 00:42:58,600
By the way,

606
00:42:59,160 --> 00:43:00,920
I've already booked the celebration dinner

607
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:02,040
for after the project wraps next week.

608
00:43:02,120 --> 00:43:03,560
Everyone's been eating
at the Celestial cafeteria for so long.

609
00:43:03,640 --> 00:43:05,080
I figured you'd want a change of pace.

610
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:06,520
Then I'm bringing
two good bottles of wine.

611
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,080
So? Are you holding up okay?

612
00:43:13,160 --> 00:43:14,920
I'm in perfect shape.

613
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:19,800
Oh my.

614
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:26,720
Let's go.

615
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:28,440
Hold on.

616
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:33,200
My nanny made this nourishing soup.

617
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:34,800
I drove home just to get it.

618
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:36,880
You're drinking all of it.
Not a single drop left.

619
00:43:38,160 --> 00:43:39,680
You drove home just to get it?

620
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:41,720
That's a whole production.

621
00:43:41,800 --> 00:43:43,840
See, I'm totally fine now. I'm good.

622
00:43:45,240 --> 00:43:46,720
It is pretty good.

623
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,240
Let's go.
